# OUTCOME MEASURE:
#   points-for under a PRIOR lineup: the season lineup is
#   chosen on a (position, positional rank) table fitted
#   leave-one-season-out, so no information about the season
#   being scored reaches it
#   TWO UPPER BOUNDS are printed beside every comparison. An
#   `oracle` lineup chosen on each player's own season mean
#   is worth +97 to +198 points a season over the prior; a
#   `hindsight` lineup chosen weekly is worth +354 to +539.
#   Any effect smaller than that spread is inside the
#   harness's own uncertainty about what a manager could
#   have known, and is not a result.
#
# THE BASELINE, and read this before anything else:
#   audible against a ten-line ADP-greedy seat with no
#   audible in it at all, paired: -31.7 [-164.5, +101.2].
